{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/write_proposal.py <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib,hashlib\nroot=pathlib.Path('/workspace');vs=json.load(open('/tmp/merge_variants.json'))\nprotocol='9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e'\nfixed=['All frozen visible fields, causal histories and sample identities','Full first-six-day training population and natural prevalence; three epochs; batch4096; history128; paired seed42 initially','Original timing modules, parameter shapes/allocation order and initialization draws','Host optimizer, loss, scorer, checkpoint-selection rule and validation population','All five appended heads, their allocation order/initialization, 33424 extra parameters, and all alternative feature computations','One shared embedding/ancestor pass; gate context is the same inherited68 coordinates']\nconf=['Different feature norms and sparsity after replacement; histogram and continuous maps are not norm matched','Shared-ancestor retraining can change optimization and learned interactions; this is not a frozen-checkpoint ensemble','A single paired seed and validation-based exploration do not establish significance or generality']\ncontrasts=[]\ndef contrast(parent,intervention,control,extra,yes,no):\n contrasts.append(dict(parent_ref=parent,intervention=intervention,control=control,held_fixed=fixed+extra,remaining_confounds=conf,decision_if_supported=yes,decision_if_not_supported=no))\ncontrast('g1-r0022-timing_joint','merge_full: preserve timing_joint and append the complete source-specific exchangeable/observed transition plus histogram, conditional mean, observed variance and third-magnitude residuals, sharing the common ancestor.','g1-r0022-timing_joint frozen source: AUC0.6306853561453415; Logloss0.1926808860955089;17253395 parameters;809.7511 wall seconds;26.3148 inference seconds. Explicitly compare on the SAME frozen validation population/seed42.',[], 'Only a gain over this stronger source is incremental utility. Require matched factorial controls and repetitions before attributing the gain to compact evidence; retain logloss and measured cost tradeoffs.','If the merge fails to beat timing_joint, incremental compact-evidence utility is unsupported for this additive implementation; retain timing_joint and inspect discriminating controls rather than calling the entire mechanism refuted.')\ncontrast('g0-r0023-shape_magnitude','merge_full versus the compact source best: does retaining the timing-specific path improve on BOTH source bests?','g0-r0023-shape_magnitude frozen source: AUC0.6232923297779764; Logloss0.1935680046323035;17204595 parameters;932.4110 wall seconds;30.2774 inference seconds. Explicitly compare the complete registered compact source config and same validation population/seed42.',[], 'Report both source comparisons separately; superiority to the weaker compact source alone is insufficient. The merge inherits all four compact readouts and its exchangeable transition, but changes allocation order relative to the standalone source after their common trunk.','Do not select a merge that only beats the compact source while losing to timing_joint. If no merge beats the stronger source, retain the stronger source as best supported measured model.')\ncontrast('g1-r0022-timing_joint','Compact-detail factor: merge_full minus merge_coarse; replicate the input replacement as merge_compact minus merge_duplicate.','merge_coarse and merge_duplicate replace the last three compact inputs with copies of the SAME ancestor64-coordinate histogram; all four compact readouts remain active and use the same inherited context gate. First histogram readout unchanged.',['Fix exchangeable transition in the first pair and duplicated chronological/product transition in the second pair.'], 'Positive compact-detail contrasts in both backgrounds, surviving paired repetitions, support utility of the combined conditional mean/variance/magnitude bundle beyond histogram readout capacity. Compute descriptive interaction (full-coarse)-(compact-duplicate).','A gain matched by coarse/histogram copies is not evidence for continuous compact detail. Opposite effects across backgrounds suggest interaction; do not average them into a universal effect. Individual moment attribution requires another study.')\ncontrast('g1-r0022-timing_joint','Exchangeable-transition factor: merge_full minus merge_compact; repeat as merge_coarse minus merge_duplicate.','merge_compact and merge_duplicate feed a duplicate of the EXISTING chronological/product1024-coordinate map into the appended transition head instead of the exchangeable/observed map.',['Fix compact-rich evidence in the first pair and repeated histogram evidence in the second pair.'], 'A positive exchangeable contrast indicates source-specific transition readout utility beyond duplicating the chronological map; inspect whether the compact-detail contrast remains necessary.','If only exchangeable additions help, do not attribute the total merge gain to compact moments. If merge_duplicate matches the full gain, extra active capacity/optimization remains a sufficient explanation.')\ncontrast('g1-r0022-timing_joint','Capacity/redundancy check: compare merge_full and each factorial cell against merge_duplicate and BOTH frozen source bests.','merge_duplicate uses only inputs already fed to timing_joint (chronological/product transitions, histogram, inherited context). It has exactly the same active head shapes and computes the same feature alternatives as merge_full.',['All cells compute rich and redundant alternatives before selection; no compute shortcut for controls.'], 'Prefer the least costly supported cell if performance is indistinguishable. Report parameters, measured train/wall/GPU cost, memory, throughput and p50/p95 including causal gathering.','If duplicated evidence reaches the same quality, reject a novel-evidence explanation. Fixed data passes are not equal-compute; no efficiency claim without a measured frontier. Do not add unequal epochs to retrofit an equal-compute result.')\nstudy=dict(id='g0-t003-shared-ancestor-merge-factorial-v1',protocol_ref=protocol,\n evidence_refs=['baseline-static','baseline-pooled','baseline-din','g0-r0023-shape_magnitude','g1-r0022-timing_joint'],\n question='Does an additive shared-ancestor merge of the complete compact-evidence branch and timing_joint outperform BOTH frozen source bests, especially timing_joint, after matching appended capacity and replacing source-specific evidence with redundant inputs?',\n hypothesis='Observed baseline AUCs are0.6050036145 static,0.6102261137 pooled and0.6133619861 DIN-style. The compact source reaches0.6232923298, while timing_joint reaches0.6306853561 (difference0.0073930264), so compact usefulness beside the stronger model is unresolved. Source slices suggest possible complementarity only exploratorily: compact empty-history AUC0.5990212 versus timing0.5906131 on8272 impressions/310 positives, and its low-history logloss is lower; overall and most large slices favor timing. Empty-history variation cannot be evidence for history moments because the new bias-free inputs are zero there. The compact source magnitude witness also loses orientation (selected feature difference about7.8e-10), so no orientation mechanism is assumed. Predict that sharing the ancestor while retaining both source-specific residual stacks may improve full-population AUC beyond timing_joint; if continuous compact detail matters, its effect should survive histogram duplication in both transition backgrounds. Source ancestry and adaptive validation selection make redundancy, extra capacity and optimization plausible alternatives.',\n nearest_work=[\n  dict(source_ref='trial://g1-r0022-timing_joint; source-sha256:426377b0677736e8505c6b3c50b780d9923617a83bf7b9dc5ec3f03ac724b9d1',verification='implementation_checked',difference='All timing classes retained verbatim except public Model renamed _FrozenTimingModel. No timing input, gap parameterization, inherited optimizer/loss or model dimension changes. The new final subclass adds the other source-specific residuals with an explicit2x2 evidence replacement.'),\n  dict(source_ref='trial://g0-r0023-shape_magnitude; source-sha256:57b762eea58bd7c3352de329412c82caaa4db87ba63faae79dfcbd94b981f883',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Inherit exchangeable/observed transition features and all four selected source maps/readout architectures: histogram, conditional within-bin mean, observed variance, absolute central third. Source feature/readout/oracle methods transplanted unchanged. Share the ancestor once with timing instead of training a second embedding model. New heads follow timing allocations, so the standalone source scratch RNG trajectory is not reproduced.'),\n  dict(source_ref='paper:din; content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2; primary text lines219-277',verification='read',difference='DIN describes target-adaptive weighted history pooling. The supplied baseline is field-adapted softmax attention, whereas DIN text explicitly abandons softmax normalization (lines270-277); it is not an exact DIN reproduction. This proposal tests deterministic compact event statistics plus timing residual complementarity, not a new attention unit. No priority/novelty claim.'),\n  dict(source_ref='paper:dmr; content-sha256:656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75; author README lines4-8',verification='read',difference='Only pinned author README is authorized/available; full publisher mechanism remains unverified. It confirms category, brand and behavior type without item identity. We add no item IDs or matching labels and make no detailed DMR comparison/reproduction claim.')],\n inherited_components=['Both frozen source configs and supplied history/feature protocol; references cite exact allowed trial IDs, source hashes and validation metrics','Exact timing source with shared field embeddings, action/log2-recency embeddings, static MLP, identity/context/repeat/overlap heads, chronological-product transition, direct/lifted gap and joint gap/endpoint-recency head','Entire compact source-specific exchangeable/observed transition and all four4256-parameter gated readouts (histogram, conditional mean, observed variance, central-third magnitude); missing-field/tied valid events remain in compact event cells','All common methods between source models are AST-identical except constructor and public forward/diagnostics; common ancestor evaluated once; no second embedding model','Original masked-event semantics, frozen coarse time thresholds, singleton-timestamp support for transitions and inherited train recipe'],\n proposed_difference='Add an independently parameterized exchangeable transition head16400 parameters and four compact gated heads17024 parameters AFTER all timing allocations: total33424 extra, expected17286819 total/208131 dense with unchanged17078688 embeddings. Compute the exact timing logit and sum five zero-initialized bias-free residuals. The2x2 controls select exchangeable versus duplicated chronological transition inputs and compact detail versus repeated ancestor histograms; all feature alternatives and heads allocate/execute equally. This is a mechanism-distinct recombination of available local sources, not a claim that its primitive statistics or residual fusion are novel. Reconstructing standalone compact predictions after joint retraining is not source checkpoint reproduction.',\n predictions=['Primary: merge_full must beat BOTH frozen source AUCs, especially0.6306853561453415 timing_joint; report the two deltas explicitly with unweighted logloss. A single-seed positive result is provisional.','Compact detail: full>coarse and compact>duplicate under matched heads; source-specific transitions: full>compact and coarse>duplicate. Report all four contrasts and their descriptive interaction, including null/negative cells.','Host diagnostic requirements: reconstructed timing logits agree with original timing forward, independent direct-cell/dense oracles agree within floating-point tolerance, logits/features finite, empty/zero-length and zero-input residuals zero, padding/input-order invariance holds.','Representational witness: ages[40000,45000,50000,55000] versus[41000,45000,50000,55000] on the same category/brand and actions[1,1,2,2] preserve inherited log2/coarse-age, transitions, gap bins and timing counts but change compact continuous statistics. Feature distinction demonstrates access only, not predictive usefulness.','Costs: added heads/moment computations may worsen measured training or inference cost. Claim quality benefit and efficiency separately; no efficiency result is predicted as certain.'],\n falsifiers=['No full-population improvement over timing_joint, even if the compact source is beaten, leaves incremental utility unsupported for this implementation.','A full gain reproduced by merge_duplicate or merge_coarse fails to support the richer compact-evidence interpretation. A transition-only effect does not establish a compact-moment effect.','No repeatable compact-detail contrast across paired seeds, unacceptable logloss degradation, or reversal in consequential adequately supported slices weakens selection.','Oracle, finite-output, timing-path reproduction or support-invariance failures invalidate the implementation comparison; they are execution failures rather than scientific counterevidence.','Measured quality gains without an acceptable cost tradeoff do not establish efficiency; inability to afford repetitions limits conclusion maturity.'],\n alternative_explanations=['Extra active nonlinear readouts, input scaling, sparsity or zero-initialization dynamics rather than new evidence','Useful exchangeable transition counts rather than conditional mean/variance/magnitude;2x2 contrasts distinguish the bundles but not each moment','Learned shared-ancestor changes and context gates, random initialization, adaptive validation selection, or user dependence','Truncated histories, undocumented as-of dates of publisher static snapshots, bucket collisions and missing fields limit external/production transfer','Small empty/rare slices can fluctuate and are exploratory; an empty-history gain comes from shared static retraining, not zero-valued new history inputs'],\n contrasts=contrasts,\n cost_plan=dict(estimate_ref='Authorized context remaining12595.3656seconds; timing source809.7511 wall/694.3669 train/26.3148 inference; compact source932.4110 wall/805.4767 train/30.2774 inference; protocol estimated unit704.373seconds; per-trial cap1760.9324seconds. New merge cost is unmeasured; use1100seconds nominal per cell, not a guarantee.',all_variants_counted=True,\n attribution_reserve='All4 seed42 factorial cells count: nominal4400seconds, hard-cap sum7043.7297seconds. Local preparation, diagnostics, failures and earlier failed proposal round24 remain charged. Round24 was rejected because both source controls were not cited/compared; it supplies no negative training evidence. This proposal explicitly cites and compares both. No screening or optimizer/loss tuning.',\n assessment_reserve='Reserve about6100seconds nominal for paired seeds43/44 of the selected merged cell, timing_joint, and closest evidence-replacement control (2*(1100+809.7511+1100) about6019.5seconds). Reuse only accepted seed42 receipts with matching hashes. Freeze selected source/config/checkpoints, comparison cells, seeds and validation commands before assessment. Repeat the standalone compact source too only if measured remaining budget permits; otherwise report omitted source repetitions. No test/withheld feedback is available or requested.',\n stop_rule='Use the host remaining ledger and caps without raising them. Before each run reserve its complete measured-cost estimate plus required comparisons. Stop at a hard limit, failed integrity, unknown execution state without reconciliation, or if no useful complete authorized experiment fits. Do not duplicate uncertain calls. If worst-case costs/preparation prevent the target repetitions, reduce the affordable validation suite explicitly and keep conclusions preliminary; never treat exhaustion as success.'))\nfor v in vs:\n h=hashlib.sha256((root/v['file']).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n v['note']=('Prospective shared-ancestor source merge2x2; both frozen controls g0-r0023-shape_magnitude and g1-r0022-timing_joint explicitly compared. '\n +f\\\"Mode transition={v['config']['merge_transition']}, evidence={v['config']['merge_evidence']}. \\\"\n +'All timing classes retained; all source compact feature/readout/oracle methods AST-identical. All cells allocate33424 appended parameters and compute all maps. Expected17286819 parameters; host must verify. '\n +f'Module SHA256={h}. Reproduce host initialization from this standalone module as Model(meta, registered config), protocol{protocol}, scratch,3epochs,batch4096,history128,seed42; host owns train/scoring/accounting. '\n +'Local checks do not execute Torch; Torch is absent. No training, installations, agents or test access. Diagnostics are candidate-supplied, bounded to64 scalars with direct/dense oracles on8 rows. '\n +'No new performance or mechanism outcome is claimed. Provenance and local check observations belong in append-only host experiment receipts; no separate writable knowledge-memory endpoint exists.')\nproposal=dict(study=study,parent_trial='g1-r0022-timing_joint',variants=vs,knowledge_assessments=[\n dict(knowledge_id='paper:din',decision='considered',rationale='Read archived primary version, including local activation and unnormalized weights; supplied DIN-style baseline differs. The merge is motivated by local source contrast rather than transplanting DIN.',transformed_mechanism='None newly adopted; existing field-adapted reference retained.',variant_names=[v['name'] for v in vs],nearest_work_difference='Deterministic source evidence recombination with matched replacement controls, not a new attention unit; priority unverified.',falsifier='If local source/control contrasts do not support complementarity, external attention results cannot rescue the claim.'),\n dict(knowledge_id='paper:dmr',decision='considered',rationale='Pinned author README read; only category, brand and behavior type, no item IDs. Publisher full mechanism unavailable; detailed nearest-work claim remains unresolved.',transformed_mechanism='No DMR module or item matching target added.',variant_names=[v['name'] for v in vs],nearest_work_difference='No detailed DMR novelty/reproduction assertion from README-only evidence.',falsifier='Any required unavailable item identity or label is outside the frozen contract and would invalidate the candidate.')])\n(root/'proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('proposal.json written; variants:',len(vs),'contrasts:',len(contrasts))\nPY\npython3 /tmp/write_proposal.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
